Algorithm

1. Start the program.
2. Create a weighted graph representing the courier hub and service areas.
3. Set the source hub distance to zero and all other distances to infinity.
4. Select the unprocessed vertex with the smallest known distance.
5. Examine all adjacent vertices of the selected vertex.
6. Add the current distance and road weight to calculate a candidate distance.
7. If the candidate distance is smaller, update the recorded distance.
8. Repeat until all reachable vertices have been processed.
9. Display the shortest distance to every reachable service area.
10. Display areas whose distances remain infinite as unreachable.
11. Stop the program.
